HST Office: Windows log off / shut down: answer WM_QUERYENDSESSION at once when nothing is unsaved.

The whole quit ran inside the WM_QUERYENDSESSION handler. Windows waits about 5 s for the answer,
then shows that an application blocks the shut down and ends the process when the user goes on (or
for an update restart). Measured on HST4 with 1.0.1 and rc/1.0.2-batch5, every document saved: the
windows closed after 0.2 s but the answer never came within the 5 s, the office reached OnCloseApp
only 98-115 s later (after the sender gave up).
- vcl salframe.cxx: on WM_QUERYENDSESSION, when no open document holds unsaved changes, the office
  answers "yes" first (ReplyMessage(TRUE), Windows goes on at once) and then quits as before.
  With unsaved changes the save question still runs inside the call (unchanged).
License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-session-end-windows-answer.py.
---
--- a/vcl/win/window/salframe.cxx
+++ b/vcl/win/window/salframe.cxx
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@
 #include <vector>
 
 #include <com/sun/star/uno/Exception.hpp>
+#include <com/sun/star/container/XEnumeration.hpp>
+#include <com/sun/star/frame/Desktop.hpp>
+#include <com/sun/star/util/XModifiable.hpp>
+#include <comphelper/processfactory.hxx>
 
 #include <oleacc.h>
 #include <com/sun/star/accessibility/XMSAAService.hpp>
@@ -4417,12 +4421,44 @@
     CloseHandle( hFile );
 }
 
+// HST Office: true when an open document holds unsaved changes, so closing it may ask the user.
+// An error counts as "yes": the caller then keeps the path that can ask.
+static bool ImplHstAnyDocumentModified()
+{
+    try
+    {
+        css::uno::Reference<css::container::XEnumeration> xComponents
+            = css::frame::Desktop::create( comphelper::getProcessComponentContext() )
+                  ->getComponents()->createEnumeration();
+        while ( xComponents->hasMoreElements() )
+        {
+            css::uno::Reference<css::util::XModifiable> xModifiable( xComponents->nextElement(),
+                                                                     css::uno::UNO_QUERY );
+            if ( xModifiable.is() && xModifiable->isModified() )
+                return true;
+        }
+    }
+    catch ( const css::uno::Exception& )
+    {
+        TOOLS_WARN_EXCEPTION( "vcl", "session end: the open documents could not be checked" );
+        return true;
+    }
+    return false;
+}
+
 static bool ImplHandleShutDownMsg( HWND hWnd )
 {
     bool nRet = false;
     WinSalFrame* pFrame = ProcessOrDeferMessage( hWnd, 0, 0, DeferPolicy::Blocked );
     if ( pFrame )
     {
+        // HST Office: Windows waits about 5 s for the answer to WM_QUERYENDSESSION, then shows
+        // that an application blocks the shut down and ends it. Quitting inside the call took
+        // 98-115 s even with every document saved: it stalls while the call is pending. With
+        // nothing to ask, answer "yes" now (ReplyMessage releases the sender) and quit afterwards;
+        // with unsaved changes the save question still runs inside the call.
+        if ( InSendMessage() && !ImplHstAnyDocumentModified() )
+            ReplyMessage( TRUE );
         nRet = pFrame->CallCallback( SalEvent::Shutdown, nullptr );
         ImplSalYieldMutexRelease();
     }
